      "side": 1,
      "message": "The rule of build-utils uses cmd_c_to_build to do the final compilation and linking, and the export_taskinfo.so.c is added to the arguments automatically (with the two object files built by cmd_to_taskinfo). Since the two object files already contain what we want, I leave the export_taskinfo.so.c empty in this final step by compiling without -DEXPORT_TASKINFO.\n\nIt is possible that we only use cmd_to_taskinfo to build RO part first, and use cmd_c_to_build to build RW part in the final step (then link with the RO part). But then there will be a risk that the build options of both parts become inconsistent. Also I need to make sure \"-DSECTION_IS_*\" is always appended at tail to override the same definition in $(BUILD_CFLAGS).",
      "parentUuid": "92801b78_69ccc50b",
